        "sha256": "a1687c4fcd05a1a1a47b8d0ef383c4490e1e247c2d673cca7c12f84ec3d17073",
        "property": "simple-match-decision-preserved",
        "claimKind": "preservation",
        "statement": "Decision preservation of PatternMatchUtils.simpleMatch(String pattern, String str) between spring-core 5.3.6 and 5.3.7 (the commits 27bfcbbc and db9a10bf, whose PatternMatchUtils.java the two releases carry unchanged): for every pattern and every str, each null or a String of at most 6 UTF-16 code units, every code unit any of the 65,536 values (an isolated surrogate, a NUL and '*' included), both revisions return the same boolean, or throw the same exception class. No allowed-change region: the patch is meant to change no decision. Nothing about case, locale or Unicode normalization is claimed; the method compares code units, and so does the claim.",
        "assume": null,
        "assert": null,
        "throws": [],
        "nullable": [
          "pattern",
          "str"
        ],
        "mayAlias": [],
        "observations": [
          "result",
          "exception"
        ],
        "assumptions": [
          {
            "text": "maxArrayLength bounds each String's length in UTF-16 code units, as the tool's own checker reads it for a String parameter (lib/README.md: a String of at most the check's bound of code units, never cut to it).",
            "basis": "The bound is part of the claim, frozen here before any attempt. 6 holds every probe shape of the brief except abcdef and xbcdef (replay only): a prefix of 3 before a star and 3 after it, two stars, and a supplementary character's surrogate pair beside a star. A proof over unbounded strings, by induction, is a separate and stronger claim."
          },
          {
            "text": "unwind 16 covers the loop and the recursion at this bound: each recursive call drops at least one code unit of pattern (the prefix branch drops firstIndex >= 1, the leading-star branches drop the star or more), so the recursion is at most 7 deep, and the while loop over str.indexOf(part) runs at most 7 times per call.",
            "basis": "Read from the method's source at both revisions (the recursion and loop structure is identical: the patch changes one expression). An unwinding the check can't complete leaves the attempt unresolved, never established."
          },
          {
            "text": "The JDK's String methods simpleMatch calls (indexOf, substring, startsWith, endsWith, equals, length, isEmpty) behave as java.lang.String specifies, on the JDK each attempt names.",
            "basis": "Both revisions call the same JDK; the claim compares them, and needs no model of these methods beyond what the checker states it reproduces, models or refuses (a gap under gaps strict is a refusal, not an assumption)."
          }
        ],
        "allowedChange": null,
